Collaborative consumption models fundamentally challenge the assumption that ownership is the primary means of accessing products. By enabling multiple users to share the same product across its lifecycle, this approach maximizes utilization rates and extends product lifespans, directly reducing per-use environmental impacts. From a design perspective, this strategy requires products to be designed for durability, cleanability, and ergonomic adaptability to diverse user needs. Products must withstand higher usage frequencies and be easily maintained between users, demanding thoughtful material selection and robust construction methods that accommodate shared stewardship.